ogles2: half-float render targets on VC4 (docs/PI3_PLAN.md §2.1,
EXT_color_buffer_half_float): the tile buffer's 64-bit colour mode, whose
pixels are RGBA16F and are stored as such (the RGBA64 texture type's texels,
patch 0018). A fragment key with color_format R16G16B16A16_FLOAT writes two
TLB words a pixel, RG then BA, each two halves (VideoCore IV guide, "Color
Read and Write"), through the per-sample colour writes (TLB_COLOR_MS acts as
TLB_COLOR_ALL without MSAA; two writes instead of four); blending reads the
two words back, unpacks the halves and blends in floats, unclamped
(vc4_do_blending_f clamps the source only for the other targets), the
colour mask per channel. No logic op, no MSAA. ntq_emit_alu handles
unpack_half_2x16 (the 16a/16b float unpack) and pack_half_2x16_split
(regfile A's 16a/16b float pack, qir_PACK_16_F). Mesa's own state never
sets the key (its screen has no such render target); v3dglslc compiles it
from keys (-k, patch 0017). Applies after 0020.

